From: PowerTune build fix <info@powertunedigital.com>
Subject: unxcfg.h: drop redundant K&R-style gmtime()/localtime() redeclaration

<time.h> (glibc and friends) already declares gmtime()/localtime() with
full prototypes. This unspecified-argument-list fallback redeclaration
was harmless under pre-C23 semantics, where empty parens meant
"unspecified parameters". Under C23 semantics (the default with newer
GCC), empty parens mean "takes no parameters", which now directly
conflicts with the real prototype and is a hard compile error:

  unxcfg.h:120:15: error: conflicting types for 'gmtime'; have 'struct tm *(void)'
  unxcfg.h:120:26: error: conflicting types for 'localtime'; have 'struct tm *(void)'

The declaration is redundant on any system with a real <time.h>, so
just drop it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [unzip 6.0 is unmaintained upstream]
Signed-off-by: PowerTune build fix <info@powertunedigital.com>

--- a/unix/unxcfg.h
+++ b/unix/unxcfg.h
@@ -117,7 +117,6 @@
 #  endif
 #else
 #  include <time.h>
-   struct tm *gmtime(), *localtime();
 #endif
 
 #if (defined(BSD4_4) || (defined(SYSV) && defined(MODERN)))
